WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:08.186 --> 00:00:09.754
Let's bring in CNN Pentagon

00:00:09.754 --> 00:00:11.756
correspondent Oren Liebermann

00:00:11.756 --> 00:00:13.758
and bring back retired colonel

00:00:13.858 --> 00:00:15.026
Cedric Layton.

00:00:15.160 --> 00:00:16.427
First, Oren, headlines out of

00:00:16.561 --> 00:00:17.862
what we just heard.

00:00:17.996 --> 00:00:20.498
&gt;&gt; General pat Ryder hit home on

00:00:20.632 --> 00:00:22.200
the point that the U.S. Seized

00:00:22.333 --> 00:00:23.234
this as international air space

00:00:23.368 --> 00:00:26.838
and the U.S. Will continue to

00:00:26.971 --> 00:00:27.772
operate there with surveillance

00:00:27.906 --> 00:00:29.808
drones and other assets as it

00:00:29.941 --> 00:00:30.675
sees fit.

00:00:30.809 --> 00:00:32.410
The U.S. Has every right to do

00:00:32.544 --> 00:00:33.778
that.

00:00:33.778 --> 00:00:35.346
Brigadier general pat rider

00:00:35.780 --> 00:00:37.448
hitting home on that point.

00:00:37.782 --> 00:00:38.750
Then asked, why release the

00:00:38.883 --> 00:00:40.084
video, and he said, the U.S.

00:00:40.218 --> 00:00:41.786
Release videos when it sees fit,

00:00:41.886 --> 00:00:43.822
after it goes through a

00:00:43.955 --> 00:00:44.455
declassification process.

00:00:44.589 --> 00:00:45.957
We were tracking this video as

00:00:46.090 --> 00:00:47.992
it was moving through that

00:00:48.126 --> 00:00:48.893
declassification process,

00:00:49.027 --> 00:00:49.427
essentially.

00:00:49.427 --> 00:00:52.263
But it also underscored that the

00:00:52.397 --> 00:00:53.865
account of the U.S. Was the one

00:00:53.998 --> 00:00:55.300
that more accurately depicted

00:00:55.433 --> 00:00:55.934
what happened here.

00:00:56.067 --> 00:00:56.901
This after the Russian

00:00:57.035 --> 00:00:58.102
ambassador to the U.S., pretty

00:00:58.236 --> 00:00:59.804
quickly after this all came out,

00:00:59.838 --> 00:01:01.272
denied that there was any

00:01:01.406 --> 00:01:01.906
contact, physical contact

00:01:02.040 --> 00:01:03.408
between the Russian and fighter

00:01:03.808 --> 00:01:04.742
jets and the drones.

00:01:04.876 --> 00:01:05.810
It was important for the U.S. To

00:01:05.810 --> 00:01:07.278
put this out there to make clear

00:01:07.412 --> 00:01:08.947
what actually happened here,

00:01:09.080 --> 00:01:12.417
Victor and bianna.

00:01:12.550 --> 00:01:14.986
And it was also note that the

00:01:15.119 --> 00:01:16.154
brigadier general said that no

00:01:16.287 --> 00:01:17.822
apology was asked for, and none

00:01:17.889 --> 00:01:18.890
was given.

00:01:19.023 --> 00:01:24.629
Not that we expect one from the

00:01:24.762 --> 00:01:26.030
Russians.

00:01:26.164 --> 00:01:27.065
But we did see whether this was

00:01:27.198 --> 00:01:28.099
a new tram.

00:01:28.233 --> 00:01:29.133
This more aggressive behavior by

00:01:29.267 --> 00:01:30.702
the rupgs military and more of

00:01:30.835 --> 00:01:32.370
these intercepts not some in the

00:01:32.503 --> 00:01:33.838
black sea, but in the middle

00:01:33.938 --> 00:01:35.006
East and in Syria.

00:01:35.139 --> 00:01:36.774
He sort of deflected that

00:01:36.908 --> 00:01:37.275
question.

00:01:37.275 --> 00:01:38.643
So I'm hoping you with your

00:01:38.776 --> 00:01:39.944
expertise can weigh in and give

00:01:40.078 --> 00:01:42.513
us your thoughts.

00:01:42.647 --> 00:01:43.248
&gt;&gt; I definitely think that that

00:01:43.381 --> 00:01:45.850
is the case, bianna.

00:01:45.950 --> 00:01:48.353
The key things here is that the

00:01:48.486 --> 00:01:49.387
Russians go in waves.

00:01:49.520 --> 00:01:50.722
Sometimes they will be much more

00:01:50.855 --> 00:01:55.927
aggressive when it comes to

00:01:56.060 --> 00:02:05.169
intercepting reconnaissance

00:02:05.303 --> 00:02:05.870
flights.

00:02:05.904 --> 00:02:06.804
With their more aggressive

00:02:06.938 --> 00:02:08.907
approach, that all changes.

00:02:09.040 --> 00:02:09.908
The rule book becomes a

00:02:10.041 --> 00:02:10.541
different one.

00:02:10.608 --> 00:02:11.876
And what the Russians end up

00:02:11.976 --> 00:02:14.012
doing is they end up taking very

00:02:14.145 --> 00:02:15.413
aggressive maneuvers against

00:02:15.546 --> 00:02:17.482
manned and unmanned areal

00:02:17.882 --> 00:02:20.051
vehicles.
And so that can have some

00:02:20.184 --> 00:02:21.886
significant consequences, not

00:02:21.953 --> 00:02:24.222
only in the black sea area, but

00:02:24.355 --> 00:02:25.490
in the baltic and other areas

00:02:25.890 --> 00:02:26.991
along the Russian border.

00:02:27.125 --> 00:02:28.660
&gt;&gt; Colonel, this drone is now

00:02:28.793 --> 00:02:32.263
under about a mile of water.

00:02:32.397 --> 00:02:34.098
Is this the retrieval worth the

00:02:34.232 --> 00:02:36.000
work for either the U.S., which

00:02:36.134 --> 00:02:38.169
says that it's unlikely they'll

00:02:38.303 --> 00:02:39.904
retrieve it, or for the

00:02:40.004 --> 00:02:41.039
Russians, who have some assets

00:02:41.172 --> 00:02:43.574
in the area and say they will go

00:02:43.908 --> 00:02:46.644
after that drone?

00:02:46.778 --> 00:02:50.682
&gt;&gt; Yeah, it's going to be hard

00:02:50.815 --> 00:02:52.517
for either side to do this,

00:02:52.650 --> 00:02:52.984
Victor.

00:02:52.984 --> 00:02:54.919
The Russians will look at it as

00:02:55.053 --> 00:02:56.387
getting a propaganda coup if

00:02:56.521 --> 00:02:59.357
they can get this up in a

00:02:59.490 --> 00:03:00.591
profitable fashion.

00:03:00.725 --> 00:03:02.427
If they can pull it up and say,

00:03:02.560 --> 00:03:04.028
look what we have, that will be

00:03:04.162 --> 00:03:05.096
a propaganda thing for them.

00:03:05.229 --> 00:03:07.498
As far as the U.S. Is concerned,

00:03:07.932 --> 00:03:08.800
you know, it would certainly be

00:03:08.933 --> 00:03:11.069
good if we could take it back,

00:03:11.202 --> 00:03:12.770
if we could get the pieces and

00:03:12.904 --> 00:03:14.739
parts that have crashed into the

00:03:14.872 --> 00:03:16.908
black sea and safeguard them

00:03:17.041 --> 00:03:18.376
from the Russians.

00:03:18.509 --> 00:03:19.944
But it is not absolutely

00:03:20.044 --> 00:03:23.982
essential that we do so.

00:03:24.115 --> 00:03:25.249
Basically, with the rendering

00:03:25.383 --> 00:03:28.419
null and void of the software

00:03:28.553 --> 00:03:30.288
that was onboard, it really

00:03:30.421 --> 00:03:31.489
takes out all of the

00:03:31.622 --> 00:03:33.057
intelligence parts that are

00:03:33.191 --> 00:03:34.025
really important that would be

00:03:34.158 --> 00:03:36.394
useful to the Russians and so if

00:03:36.527 --> 00:03:38.363
that is true, they were able to

00:03:38.496 --> 00:03:41.966
in essence zero all the data

00:03:41.966 --> 00:03:43.134
that was important and it's not

